!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-constructor-may-not-declare-a-chain-field-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.1"
  description: """
    Every type constructor composes the kernel's `chained`, through `type`, so it already has a field
    named `chain`: the IS-A chain the resolver computes, which no declaration writes. A constructor
    declaring a field of that name is refused where it is declared, rather than when an instance first
    uses it.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["meta.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
